$$

for some integers $x$ and $y$ with $x>\sqrt{a}$. Denote by $B$ the set of all positive integers $k$ such that (1) is satisfied for some integers $x$ and $y$ with $0 \leqslant x<\sqrt{a}$. Prove that $A=B$.

