solution:
Since the terms are nonzero, we can define $a_{n}=\left(x_{n+1}+x_{n-1}\right) / x_{n}$ for $n \geq 1$. It suffices to show $a_{1}=a_{2}=\cdots$. But $x_{n+1}^{2}-x_{n} x_{n+2}=1=x_{n}^{2}-x_{n-1} x_{n+1}$,

